# Environment files. `.env*`, not a bare `.env`: that pattern left
# .env.prd — real prod SECRET_KEY, DB password, Zoho and OpenAI keys —
# untracked but NOT ignored, one `git add .` away from entering history
# permanently. The negation keeps committing a redacted .env.example
# possible without reopening the hole.
.env*
!.env.example
.log
# Runtime logs. These were tracked, which meant a deploy that resets prod's
# checkout to the shipped commit would overwrite logs/daphne.log while daphne
# still held it open — the writes then go to an unlinked inode and vanish.
# logs/ itself stays in the tree via .gitkeep: settings.LOGGING points a
# FileHandler at logs/vat_pipeline.log, and FileHandler creates the file but
# not the directory, so an absent logs/ is a startup failure.
logs/*.log
*.sqlite3
merilv_test_report_2026-08-30.xlsx
dummy_login_vendorlink.txt
media/
__pycache__/
req/
# Dummy/sample design references and mock upload templates. The directory on
# disk is spelled "dummy_tempelate" (el transposed) — the correctly-spelled
# rules below matched nothing for as long as they existed, which is how the
# dummy PDFs/XLSX ended up tracked. Both spellings are covered now.
dummy_tempelate/
dummy_template/
dummy_template
*.pyc
translation_sessions.json
SA_README.html
module_info/
# SQL dump files — never commit raw DB exports
*.sql
schema_backup.sql
data_backup.sql
migrations.zip

