# nginx was only used by the old local-dev compose topology (nginx :8443 +
# TLS termination in front of Daphne). The current docker-compose.yml runs
# Daphne directly on host networking with no nginx service, and this folder
# isn't present on manas either — it's dead config, and its cert/key pair
# should never have been committed in the first place.
nginx/

# Database dumps. Four of these (23 MB) had been committed: they are point-in-
# time copies of the production-shaped database, including vendor contact
# rows, and version control is the wrong place for either the bulk or the
# contents. Kept on disk, untracked from here on.
backups/
*.dump
*.sql.gz

# Scratch output from local verification runs — screenshots, rendered page
# dumps and the stray NUL that Windows redirection leaves behind.
tmp_vlshots/
tmp_vlshots*
NUL

# CI code-quality output. scripts/ci-quality.sh regenerates it; published as
# job artifacts rather than committed.
quality-reports/

# ── Tracked-by-accident scratch, untracked 2026-09-18 ──────────────────────
# A .gitignore rule does nothing to a file git is already tracking, which is
# how all of these stayed in every clone and every checkout despite the rules
# above matching their names. They were untracked with `git rm --cached` (the
# files stay on disk) and these patterns stop them coming back.

# One-off debugging scripts from the jabalpur serial investigation. The
# existing /jab1.py rule matched one of four.
/jab_default_serial_bug.py
/jab_verify_raw.py
/jab_verify_raw2.py
/raw.py
/xrule.py
/build_verification_report.py

# Generated exports and one-off verification reports. Each is a point-in-time
# artifact of a run that has long finished; the code that produces them is
# what belongs in the repository.
/merilv_verification_*.xlsx
/vendorlink_price_premium_heatmap.xlsx
/Meril-V courier by region.xlsx

# Local scratch: dumps pulled for a bug, barcode captures, generated masters.
# pytest already skips tmp/ (see norecursedirs in pytest.ini).
tmp/
docs/Dumps/

# ── 2026-09-21 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dummy design references and mock upload templates. The `dummy_tempelate/`
# rule above has matched since it was written, but a .gitignore rule does
# nothing to a file git is ALREADY tracking — so all ten (1.7 MB of sample
# PDFs, XLSX and DOCX) stayed in every clone. Untracked with
# `git rm -r --cached dummy_tempelate`; the files stay on disk and the rule
# above now keeps them out.

# logs/ contents are ignored above, but this one file must stay tracked:
# settings.LOGGING points a FileHandler at logs/, and FileHandler creates the
# file but NOT the directory — an absent logs/ is a startup failure. Note the
# rule above is `logs/*`, not `logs/`: excluding the DIRECTORY would make this
# negation a no-op, because git will not descend into an excluded directory to
# re-include something inside it.
!logs/.gitkeep

# Word documents, for the same reason *.pptx is ignored: handover decks and
# scope documents are shared, not versioned here.
*.docx

